{"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/calling-functions-with-pointer-parameters"},"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"patch":0,"minor":3},"kind":"article","sections":[],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/swift\/calling-functions-with-pointer-parameters"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","anchor":"Overview","level":2,"text":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"When calling a function that takes a pointer as a parameter, you can use implicit"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"casting to pass a compatible pointer type or implicit bridging to pass a pointer"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"to a variable or the contents of an array."}]},{"type":"heading","anchor":"Pass-a-Constant-Pointer-as-a-Parameter","level":3,"text":"Pass a Constant Pointer as a Parameter"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"When you call a function that is declared as taking an ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"UnsafePointer<Type>"},{"text":" argument,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"you can pass any of the following:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"An "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"UnsafePointer<Type>"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"UnsafeMutablePointer<Type>"},{"type":"text","text":", or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AutoreleasingUnsafeMutablePointer<Type>"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"value, which is implicitly cast to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"UnsafePointer<Type>"},{"type":"text","text":" as necessary."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"String"},{"text":" value, if ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Type"},{"text":" is ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Int8"},{"type":"text","text":" or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"UInt8"},{"type":"text","text":". The string is automatically converted"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"to UTF8 in a zero-terminated buffer, and a pointer to that buffer is passed to the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"function."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"An in-out expression that contains a mutable variable, property, or subscript reference"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"of type "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Type"},{"text":", which is passed as a pointer to the address of the left-hand side","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"identifier.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"[Type]"},{"text":" value, which is passed as a pointer to the start of the array.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The pointer you pass to the function is only guaranteed to be valid for the duration"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"of the function call. Do not persist the pointer and access it after the function"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"has returned."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"This example shows the different ways that you can call the a function that takes"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"a constant pointer:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["func takesAPointer(_ p: UnsafePointer<Float>) {","    \/\/ ...","}","","var x: Float = 0.0","takesAPointer(&x)","takesAPointer([1.0, 2.0, 3.0])"],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"When you call a function that takes an "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"UnsafeRawPointer"},{"type":"text","text":" argument, you can pass"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the same operands as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"UnsafePointer<Type>"},{"type":"text","text":", but with any type as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Type"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"This example shows the different ways that you can call a function that takes a constant"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"raw pointer:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["func takesARawPointer(_ p: UnsafeRawPointer?)  {","    \/\/ ...","}","","var x: Float = 0.0, y: Int = 0","takesARawPointer(&x)","takesARawPointer(&y)","takesARawPointer([1.0, 2.0, 3.0] as [Float])","let intArray = [1, 2, 3]","takesARawPointer(intArray)","takesARawPointer(\"How are you today?\")"],"type":"codeListing"},{"anchor":"Pass-a-Mutable-Pointer-as-a-Parameter","level":3,"text":"Pass a Mutable Pointer as a Parameter","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"When you call a function that is declared as taking an "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"UnsafeMutablePointer<Type>"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"argument, you can pass any of the following:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"An "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"UnsafeMutablePointer<Type>"},{"type":"text","text":" value."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"An in-out expression of type "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Type"},{"type":"text","text":" that contains a mutable variable, property,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"or subscript reference, which is passed as a pointer to the address of the mutable"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"value."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"An in-out expression of type "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"[Type]"},{"type":"text","text":" that contains a mutable variable, property,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"or subscript reference, which is passed as a pointer to the start of the array, and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"is lifetime-extended for the duration of the call."}]}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"This example shows the different ways that you can call a function that takes a mutable"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"pointer:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["func takesAMutablePointer(_ p: UnsafeMutablePointer<Float>) {","    \/\/ ...","}","","var x: Float = 0.0","var a: [Float] = [1.0, 2.0, 3.0]","takesAMutablePointer(&x)","takesAMutablePointer(&a)"],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"When you call a function that is declared as taking an "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"UnsafeMutableRawPointer"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"argument, you can pass the same operands as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"UnsafeMutablePointer<Type>"},{"type":"text","text":", but for"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"any type as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Type"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"This example shows the different ways that you can call a function that takes a mutable"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"raw pointer:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["func takesAMutableRawPointer(_ p: UnsafeMutableRawPointer?)  {","    \/\/ ...","}","","var x: Float = 0.0, y: Int = 0","var a: [Float] = [1.0, 2.0, 3.0], b: [Int] = [1, 2, 3]","takesAMutableRawPointer(&x)","takesAMutableRawPointer(&y)","takesAMutableRawPointer(&a)","takesAMutableRawPointer(&b)"],"type":"codeListing"},{"anchor":"Pass-an-Autoreleasing-Pointer-as-a-Parameter","level":3,"text":"Pass an Autoreleasing Pointer as a Parameter","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"When you call a function that is declared as taking an "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AutoreleasingUnsafeMutablePointer<Type>"},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"you can pass any of the following:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"An "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AutoreleasingUnsafeMutablePointer<Type>"},{"type":"text","text":" value."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"An in-out expression that contains a mutable variable, property, or subscript reference"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"of type "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Type"},{"type":"text","text":". The value of the operand is copied bitwise into a temporary nonowning"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"buffer. The address of that buffer is passed to the callee, and on return, the value"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"in the buffer is loaded, retained, and reassigned into the operand."}]}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Unlike with other pointer types, you can’t use an array as an implicitly bridged"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"parameter."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Pass-a-Function-Pointer-as-a-Parameter","level":3,"text":"Pass a Function Pointer as a Parameter","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"When calling a function that takes a C function pointer argument, you can pass a","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"top-level Swift function, a closure literal, a closure declared with the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@convention(c)"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"attribute, or ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"nil"},{"type":"text","text":". You can also pass a closure property of a generic type or a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"generic method as long as no generic type parameters are referenced in the closure’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"argument list or body."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"For example, consider Core Foundation’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"CFArrayCreateMutable(_:_:_:)"},{"type":"text","text":" function."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"The "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"CFArrayCreateMutable(_:_:_:)"},{"type":"text","text":" function takes a "},{"code":"CFArrayCallBacks","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" structure,","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"which is initialized with function pointer callbacks:"}]},{"syntax":"swift","code":["func customCopyDescription(_ p: UnsafeRawPointer?) -> Unmanaged<CFString>? {","    \/\/ return an Unmanaged<CFString>? value","}","","var callbacks = CFArrayCallBacks(","    version: 0,","    retain: nil,","    release: nil,","    copyDescription: customCopyDescription,","    equal: { (p1, p2) -> DarwinBoolean in","        \/\/ return Bool value","    }",")","var mutableArray = CFArrayCreateMutable(nil, 0, &callbacks)"],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"In this example, the ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"CFArrayCallBacks"},{"text":" initializer uses ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"nil"},{"type":"text","text":" values as arguments"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"for the ","type":"text"},{"code":"retain","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"release"},{"type":"text","text":" parameters, the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"customCopyDescription(_:)"},{"text":" function","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"as the argument for the ","type":"text"},{"code":"customCopyDescription","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" parameter, and a closure literal","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"as the argument for the ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"equal"},{"text":" parameter.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Only Swift function types with C function reference calling convention may","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"be used for function pointer arguments. Like a C function pointer, a Swift function","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"type with the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@convention(c)"},{"text":" attribute does not capture the context of its surrounding","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"scope.","type":"text"}]}],"style":"note","name":"Note","type":"aside"}]}],"metadata":{"roleHeading":"Article","title":"Calling Functions With Pointer Parameters","role":"article","modules":[{"name":"Swift"}]},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift","doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/swift-standard-library","doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/manual-memory-management"]]},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Use implicit pointer casting or bridging when calling functions that takes pointers"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"as parameters."}],"references":{"doc://com.apple.Swift/documentation/Swift":{"role":"collection","abstract":[{"text":"Build apps using a powerful open language.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/swift","title":"Swift","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift","type":"topic","kind":"symbol"},"doc://com.apple.Swift/documentation/Swift/manual-memory-management":{"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/manual-memory-management","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Allocate and manage memory manually."}],"url":"\/documentation\/swift\/manual-memory-management","title":"Manual Memory Management","kind":"article","role":"collectionGroup"},"doc://com.apple.Swift/documentation/Swift/swift-standard-library":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Solve complex problems and write high-performance, readable code."}],"type":"topic","kind":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/swift-standard-library","url":"\/documentation\/swift\/swift-standard-library","title":"Swift Standard Library","role":"collectionGroup"}}}